      "feedback": "Toxicity Verification: Verified. True palms of the genus Livistona contain no toxic systemic alkaloids or saponins for dogs or cats. It is rated Green with an appropriate physical safety warning regarding its armed petiolar teeth.Florida Cold-Hardiness: Mature specimens are exceptionally cold-hardy, safely handling temps down to $25^\\circ\\text{F}$ (Zone 9b). This makes it a bulletproof planting choice for Bradenton's winter fluctuations.Airtight Science: By eliminating the obsolete \"ancient Gondwanan relic\" narrative and focusing on the Aboriginal anthropochory (human transport) discovery, we present world-class, up-to-date science that sets a stellar example of botanical park curation.\n\n\nThe Red Cabbage Palm (Livistona mariae)—known also as the Central Australian Fan Palm—is a spectacular addition to Palma Sola Botanical Park. It carries one of the most astonishing evolutionary and cultural origin stories in the entire plant kingdom.\n\nTo represent our park with the highest standard of",
